 {
  "id": "TS3006c.sys.s.27",
  "text": "Key design decisions were identified: kinetic energy source, pushbuttons, a single curved design compromise, use of the advanced chip, product name Real Remote, outsourcing production to China, and a compromise toward a single curved design to appeal to all; plus problems including PowerPoint difficulties, time constraints, unclear cost/feasibility (target price 25 Euro), indoor solar feasibility concerns, asset limitations in slides, concerns about child labour in China's manufacturing, and color accessibility/readability for colorblind users.",
